# Copy, Claims & Content

## Privacy Claims Are Load-Bearing

The App Store privacy label is published as **"Data Not Collected"**, and `/privacy.html` is the privacy URL on the App Store listing. Site copy is a compliance surface, not just marketing. Every claim must be true of the shipping app:

- Free — no ads, no account, no subscription, no credits (all IAP removed from sale as of 4.0)
- Notes never leave the device except to sync through the user's own private iCloud
- Search, answers, and understanding run on-device with Apple Intelligence
- Every context signal has an off switch

**Never add a claim the app doesn't back.** If a feature changes what leaves the device, `/privacy.html` and the `#privacy` section on the landing page change in the same commit.

One distinction to keep straight: **Pro Mode** (bring-your-own-key web search, opt-in, off by default) is the single path that sends note text and photos off-device, and only on an explicit user action. It is not the same as capture-time understanding, which is always on-device. Don't blur the two in copy.

## Positioning

- "A notebook, not a database" — no folders, no tags to manage, no sorting
- Retrieval by memory: "coffee shop notes," "rainy day ideas," "notes from Traverse City"
- Calm and emptiness are the point. Don't write dashboard or productivity-tool copy.

## Platform Copy — Check Before Propagating

Current copy says "on your iPhone" throughout — hero, `.fine` line, `#privacy`, meta descriptions, and og tags. **A native Mac app now ships**, so any edit touching those lines should reconsider the iPhone-only phrasing rather than copying it forward.

## Adding a Blog Post

Create `public/blog/<slug>.html`, then three updates or the post is orphaned:

1. A `<li>` in `public/blog/index.html` → `.postlist`, with `.date`, `.title` link, and `.excerpt`
2. A `<url>` entry in `public/sitemap.xml` with `<lastmod>` and `<priority>0.7</priority>`
3. The post's own `<title>`, `meta description`, and og tags

Link to posts **extensionless**: `/blog/<slug>`, never `/blog/<slug>.html`.

## Per-Page Requirements

- `<title>` suffixed `— Musing`, plus a real `meta name="description"`
- Open Graph: `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` (absolute `https://musingnotes.app/og-card.png`), `og:url`
- `<html lang="en" data-theme="foolscap">`
- Decorative glyphs (`⚙`, `◉`, `︿`, dot spans) get `aria-hidden="true"`; interactive swatches keep `aria-pressed` and `role="tablist"` on the picker
